                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to im_n(f)
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      induces an
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                      on
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
                      in degree
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
                  %li
                    %p
                      induces an
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                      on
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
                      in degree
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo &lt;
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt n-1
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi im
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im_n(f) \to Y
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      induces a
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                      on
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
                      in degree
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
                  %li
                    %p
                      induces an
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                      on
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
                      in degree
                      = succeed "." do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mo ≥
                              %mi n
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq n
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine"}> Goerss-Jardine, def. VI 2.9
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n-connected%2C+n-truncated%29+factorization+system"} (n-connected, n-truncated) factorization system
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              regarded as a morphism in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-epimorphism"} n-epimorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-monomorphism"} n-monomorphism
              factorization through the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-image"} n-image
              of a morphism.
          %h3#DefinitionForSimplicialPresheaves For simplicial presheaves
          %h2#constructions Constructions
          %p We discuss explicit constructions/presentations of Postnikov systems.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#ConStructionForSimplicialSets"} For simplicial sets
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a{:href => "#ForStrctOmegaGroupoids"} For strict ω-groupoids
                \.
          %h3#ConStructionForSimplicialSets For simplicial sets
          %p
            There are three main functorial models for the Postnikov tower of a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a{:href => "#CoskeletonTower"} Coskeleton tower
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a{:href => "#IdentificationRelativeSkeleta"} Identification relative to skeleta
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#HomotopyClassesRelativeSkeleta"} Homotopy classes relative to skeleta
          %h4#CoskeletonTower Coskeleton tower
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is regarded as an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              modeled as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coskeleton"} coskeleton
              sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi cosk
                      %mi n
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi cosk
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi cosk
                      %mi n
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\lim_n
                    \\big(
                    cosk_n X \to \cdots \to cosk_{n+1} X \to cosk_{n} X \to \cdots \to *
                    \\big)
            %p
              exhibits a Postnikov tower for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This is observed for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#ArtinMazur"}> ArtinMazur
            ) or (
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKan"}> DwyerKan
            ). Also see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coskeleton"} coskeleton
            for more details.
          %h4#IdentificationRelativeSkeleta Identification relative to skeleta
          %p
            The following construction quotients out the relations encoded by the cells that are thrown in in the above construction, such as to make the maps in the Postnikov tower into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
          %p We first discuss the absolute tower and then the relative version.
          %h5#absolute_postnikov_tower Absolute Postnikov tower
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim_n
              on the simplices of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as follows: two
              = succeed "-simplices" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %mi β
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi q
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\alpha, \beta : \Delta^q \to X
            %p
              are equivalent if their restriction to the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+skeleton"} skeleton
              coincides
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sk
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi sk
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi sk
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi q
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sk_n(\alpha) = sk_n(\beta)
                    \:
                    sk_n(\Delta^q)
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    \\Delta^q
                    \\to X
                    \\,.
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∼
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X(n) := X/_{\sim_n}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
          %p There are evident morphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X(n) \to X(n-1).
          #SimplPostnikovByCoskeletonQuotient.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              This is a Postnikov tower, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialPostnikovTower"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
            %p Moreover the canonical morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ←
                          %mi n
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to \lim_{\leftarrow_n} X(n)
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+limit"}> inverse limit
              ”) over this tower diagram.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine"}> Goerss-Jardine, theorem Vi 2.5
            ).
          %h5#RelativePostnikovTowerConstruction Relative Postnikov tower
          %p
            We discuss a model for the relative Postnikov tower, def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialPostnikovTowerRelative"}
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              between
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim_n
              on
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\alpha, \beta \colon \Delta^k \to X
            %p
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi n
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \sim_n \beta
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleta"} skeleta
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi sk
                          %mi n
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi k
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi k
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi α
                            %mo ,
                            %mi β
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sk_n \Delta^k \to \Delta^k \stackrel{\alpha, \beta}{\to} X
                  are equal;
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/images"} images
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\alpha), f(\beta)\in Y
                  are equal.
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi im
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    im_{n+1}(f) \coloneqq X/\sim_n
            %p
              be the simplicial set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              under this equivalence relation.
            %p
              This canonically comes with morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi im
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi im
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im_{n_1}(f) \to im_{n_2}(f)
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ≥
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                      %mo &gt;
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty \geq n_1 \gt n_2 \geq 0
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine"}> Goerss-Jardine, def. VI 2.9
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              This construction gives indeed a relative Postnikov tower for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine"}> Goerss-Jardine, theorem VI 2.11
            ).
          %h4#HomotopyClassesRelativeSkeleta Homotopy classes relative to skeleta
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mrow
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi n
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{\lt n}X
            be the simplicial set defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mrow
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi m
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi k
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi homotopy
                  %mo −
                  %mi rel
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi skeleton
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau_{\lt m}X : k \mapsto X_k / homotopy-rel-(n-1)-skeleton
                  \\,,
          %p
            where two
            = succeed "-cells" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            between them that fixes their
            = succeed "-skeleton." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
          %p
            This is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Duskin"} John Duskin
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Beke"} Beke, pages 302-305
          %h3#ForStrictOmegaGroupoids
            For strict
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Consider an object in
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              that is in the image of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Str
                      %mi ω
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Str\omega Grpd
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} strict ∞-groupoids
            %p
              Then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the
              = succeed "-Postnikov" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} strict ∞-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi im
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im_n(f)
              with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi im
                          %mi n
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi f
                          %mo )
                        %mo )
                      %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mi k
                            %mtd
                              %mo ∀
                              %mi k
                              %mo &lt;
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi im
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⊂
                              %msub
                                %mi Y
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mo ∀
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi k
                              %mo =
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mo ∀
                              %mi k
                              %mo ≥
                              %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(im_n\left(f\right)\right)_k
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    X_k &amp; \forall  k \lt n-1
                    \\\
                    im(X_{n-1}) \subset Y_{n-1} &amp; \forall \; k = n-1
                    \\\
                    \\ast &amp; \forall  k \geq n
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p
              equipped with the evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              operations induced from those of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              = succeed "-groupoids" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi im
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to im_n(f) \to \ast
            %p
              (the left one being the identity in degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \lt n-1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≥
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \geq n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \lt n-1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
              and the identity in degree
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≥
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \geq n
          %p
            This is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#BFGM"}> BFGM
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
              of a strict
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              are simply given by the groups of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
              of the identity
              = succeed "-morphism" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k-1)
              = succeed "-morphisms" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k+1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
              in that degree). Therefore it is clear from the construction of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi im
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im_n(f)
              above that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi im
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to im_n(f)
              is surjective on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
              and an isomorphism on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{k \lt n-1}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi im
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im_n(f)
              is a monomorphism on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{n-1}
              and an isomorphism on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ≥
                          %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{k \geq n}
          %h3#ExamplesForChainComplexes For chain complexes
          %p
            The following gives a model for the
            = succeed "-stage" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
            between
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
          %p
            Before we give the explicit formule below as prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ImageFactorizationForChainComplexes"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ChainComplexnPlusOneImageInDegreen"}
            motivates the formula by regarding chain complexes as models for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} strict ∞-groupoids
            (by this prop.orrespondence#GlobularAndCubical))
          #ChainComplexnPlusOneImageInDegreen.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\bullet \colon V_\bullet \longrightarrow W_\bullet
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi im
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi coker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (im_{n+1}(f))_n
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    coker(\,
                    ker(\partial_V) \cap ker(f_n)
                    \\to
                    V_n
                    \\,)
            %p For the following it is helpful to think of this abelian group in the following equivalent ways.
            %p
              Define an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_n
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi v
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mi n
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi V
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi V
                      %mi v
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mtext and
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    v_n \sim v'_n
                    \\right)
                    \\;\Leftrightarrow\;
                    \\left(
                    (\partial_V v_n = \partial_V v'_n)
                    \\;\text{and}\;
                    (f_n(v_n) = f_n(v'_n))
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p Then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi im
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (im_{n+1}(f))_n \simeq V_n/_\sim
            %p
              is equivalently the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              of this equivalence relation, which inherits abelian group structure since the eqivalence relation is linear.
            %p This is because the equivalence relation says equivalently that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi v
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mi n
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi v
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mi n
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    v_n \sim v'_n
                    \\right)
                    \\;\Leftrightarrow\;
                    \\left(
                    v_n - v'_n \;\in\; ker(\partial_V) \cap ker(f_n)
                    \\right)
            %p and hence is generated under linearity by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∼
                      %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    v_n \sim 0
                    \\right)
                    \\;\Leftrightarrow\;
                    \\left(
                    v_n  \in ker(\partial_V) \cap ker(f_n)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, notice that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi DK
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi KanCplx
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    DK
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Ch_{\bullet \geq 0}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    KanCplx
            %p
              factors through
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globe"} globular
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+omega-groupoids"} strict omega-groupoids
              (
              %a{:href => "Dold-Kan+correspondence#GlobularAndCubical"}> here
              ). An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-morphism"} n-morphism
              in the
